li.t:
the supported tasks, their required exact Core claims and Coverage
        claims, whether the task ranges over selected actions or the full
        population, and the basis for any required exhaustive enumeration;

the required compatibility of scopes, epochs, recipients, logical
        cutoffs, evaluation contexts, trust configurations, and policies,
        including any additional transformation or correspondence premises;
        equal identifiers alone do not establish compatible meanings;

section.t:
Creation completeness requires a B-related candidate for each A element;
      creation soundness requires a B-related A element for each C candidate;
      creation exactness requires the bijection and no unresolved identity
      conflict. Two valid receipt UUIDs for one action can preserve completeness
      and soundness while refuting exactness.

